The filename `--spaces in this filename--` has two problems: spaces, which the shell treats as separators, and leading `--`, which the shell interprets as a flag rather than a filename. Prefixing with `./` forces the shell to treat it as a file path, and wrapping in quotes handles the spaces, giving us `cat './--spaces in this filename--'`.


