`find` searches for files in a directory hierarchy based on conditions you specify.
Basic syntax: `find <where> <what>`

Key flags:
| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `-type f` | Search for files only (use `-type d` for directories) |
| `-name` | Search by filename e.g. `-name "*.txt"` |
| `-size` | Search by size e.g. `-size 1033c` (c=bytes, k=kilobytes, M=megabytes) |
| `! -executable` | Exclude executable files (`!` means NOT) |
| `-user` | Search by owner e.g. `-user bandit7` |
| `-group` | Search by group e.g. `-group bandit6` |
| `-readable` | Only human-readable files |
| `2>/dev/null` | Suppresses "Permission denied" errors from the output |


